-- hello.lut: the first program with an action (10.S2, D8). `main` takes the world and gives it
-- back with its result; the action is the host's `print`, an extern of world_model.lut, which
-- runs when a demand reaches `main` and never from a memo (10.S6); its description, `console` of
-- the same file, is what world.lth's laws test.

import "world_model.lut" HostConsole host : HostConsole

main (w : W) : W * Unit := host.print w "hello, world"
